The location setup seems cool: it uses GPS (remote) and a scanner (local). Basically, when people pass by a specific point in the city, the scanner detects them. It uses both GPS and the scanner; if the scanner misses someone or fails to identify them, the GPS kicks in to count the people at those coordinates. So, if there are 8 people present but the scanner only counts 7, the one not identified is flagged and penalized.

